<section>
  <div class="container content">
    <h2>Gold Mining in Australia</h2>
    <p>Australia is one of the great goldfields of the world. The Victorian rushes of the 1850s around Ballarat and Bendigo rivaled California, the Western Australian fields built Kalgoorlie, and the Pilbara has produced spectacular nugget finds in recent years. Across Victoria, Western Australia, Queensland, and New South Wales, alluvial and placer ground still holds recoverable gold for operators with the right equipment.</p>
    <p>We build wash plants in the USA and ship them container-ready to Australia. The plant is engineered to load into shipping containers, sail to a major Australian port, and set up on site in about 30 minutes. We handle export documentation and freight coordination; our guide to <a href="/blog/shipping-gold-wash-plant-internationally/">shipping a wash plant internationally</a> walks through the full process.</p>
    <p>Because ocean freight is a fixed cost, most Australian buyers choose a larger plant to make the shipment worthwhile. Our guide to <a href="/blog/buying-gold-wash-plant-from-usa/">buying a wash plant from the USA</a> covers what international buyers should know, and the <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-cost-guide/">cost guide</a> helps you budget.</p>
  </div>
</section>

