    <h2>Australia Mining Questions</h2>
    <h3>How do you ship a gold wash plant to Australia?</h3>
    <p>Our wash plants are built container-ready and shipped by sea to major Australian ports including Fremantle, Melbourne, and Brisbane. We handle export documentation and coordinate freight; you arrange customs clearance and final delivery to your site.</p>
    <h3>What size gold wash plant is right for an Australian operation?</h3>
    <p>Because international freight is a fixed cost, most Australian buyers choose a 100, 200, or 300 ton plant to make the shipment worthwhile. We help you match capacity to your ground and goldfield.</p>
    <h3>What about import duties and customs for Australia?</h3>
    <p>Customs clearance and any import duties are handled by the buyer on arrival. We provide complete commercial and export documentation to make clearance straightforward.</p>
    <h3>How long does it take to get a wash plant to Australia?</h3>
    <p>Build time is typically one to three weeks, followed by ocean transit to your chosen Australian port. We give you a full timeline with your quote.</p>
